        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0584" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg562"/>

                <head>No. 97.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 8, 1872</date>.
                        (Received June 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith copies
                    of all the correspondence which has taken place between Lord Granville and
                    myself relative to the proposed new Treaty Article in regard to indirect claims,
                    since the 31st ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed>
                </closer>













